{"sequence":14,"at":"2026-09-30T21:15:19.562Z","kind":"response","attemptId":"provider-attempt-7","phase":"initial","transport":"schema-tool","attempt":{"id":"provider-attempt-7","phase":"initial","transport":"schema-tool","status":"response","startedAt":"2026-09-30T21:14:16.180Z","request":{"messageCount":11,"messageCharacters":43916,"toolNames":["source_list","source_search","source_symbol","source_read","skill_reference_read"],"maxTokens":6000,"executableTools":true,"toolSchemas":[{"type":"object","properties":{"offset":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"required":[],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string"},"path":{"type":"string"},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"required":["text"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["name"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"startLine":{"type":"integer","minimum":1},"endLine":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"required":["path","startLine","endLine"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"additionalProperties":false}]},"usage":{"input":6105,"output":2607,"cacheRead":17920,"cacheWrite":0},"costUsd":null,"transportAttempts":"unknown","response":{"text":"## Conformance result\n\n**The document-notes operation is not compliant with the supplied policy.** Both GET and POST enforce the required permission names in some branches, but the object-level helper treats document ownership—and an unowned document—as sufficient authorization. The independent policy explicitly states that ownership does not substitute for the required object grant.\n\n### Policy under review\n\n- **GET/viewing notes:** requires a `view_document` grant on the addressed document.\n- **POST/creating a note:** requires a `change_document` grant on the addressed document.\n- **Ownership alone is not a substitute** for either grant.\n- The document owner is unspecified, and no object grants are supplied; those branches therefore remain conditional below.\n\n## Endpoint and operation trace\n\nThe named operation is the `notes` detail action on `DocumentViewSet`. It supports GET, POST, and DELETE and assigns `PaperlessNotePermissions` at the action level【ev-b56db6f459d806989798†L1841-L1848】. Its documentation describes the operation as viewing, adding, or deleting document notes【ev-1f6986adf2660dead666†L855-L856】.\n\nThe action loads the addressed document by `pk`; a nonexistent document produces `404`【ev-b56db6f459d806989798†L1849-L1864】. The supplied URL excerpt establishes the documents API prefix【ev-9c181191397fa6144f99†L140-L147】, but the provided source evidence does not include the router registration needed to state the complete concrete URL pattern independently.\n\nThe action-level permission class requires authenticated users and applies these model-level permissions:\n\n- GET: `documents.view_note` and `documents.view_document`\n- POST: `documents.add_note`, `documents.view_document`, and `documents.change_document`【ev-190e8df9a1f470ae174d†L673-L699】\n\nThese are endpoint gates, but the relevant document-specific checks occur inside the action.\n\n## GET — viewing notes\n\n### Source path and effect\n\nAfter loading the addressed document, GET performs an owner-aware `view_document` check:\n\n```python\nif currentUser is not None and not has_perms_owner_aware(\n    currentUser,\n    \"view_document\",\n    doc,\n):\n    return HttpResponseForbidden(...)\n```\n\n【ev-b56db6f459d806989798†L1851-L1862】\n\nIf the check passes, the action serializes the document's notes and returns them in the response【ev-b56db6f459d806989798†L1866-L1871】. The serializer exposes each note's ID, text, creation time, and user information【ev-b053b531fa299251e921†L990-L996】. Thus, the protected effect is disclosure of the addressed document's notes.\n\n### Owner/grant branches\n\nThe helper used by this check is:\n\n```python\nreturn obj.owner is None or obj.owner == user or checker.has_perm(perms, obj)\n```\n\n【ev-190e8df9a1f470ae174d†L624-L635】\n\nTherefore, for GET:\n\n| Addressed document state | `view_document` object grant | Result under source behavior | Supplied-policy result |\n|---|---:|---|---|\n| Owner is unspecified | Unspecified | Cannot resolve definitively. If owner is `None`, the helper allows access without a grant. | Must require the grant; ownership/unowned status cannot substitute. |\n| Owned by current user | Absent | Allowed because `obj.owner == user`. | **Should be denied** absent a `view_document` grant. |\n| Owned by another user | Present | Allowed through the object grant. | Allowed. |\n| Owned by another user | Absent | Denied by the method-level check, assuming the request reaches it. | Denied. |\n\n### GET conformance\n\n**Noncompliant.** The implementation does require a `view_document` grant for the non-owner branch, but it also allows:\n\n1. the current user who owns the document, without the grant; and\n2. an unowned document, without the grant.\n\nBoth outcomes conflict with the supplied rule that viewing notes always requires a `view_document` grant and that ownership does not substitute for it.\n\nThe action-level requirement for `documents.view_document` is not sufficient to cure this: the policy concerns a grant on the addressed object, while the shown permission class checks the request user's model-level permissions【ev-190e8df9a1f470ae174d†L678-L699】.\n\n## POST — creating a note\n\n### Source path and effect\n\nPOST first performs the same owner-aware `view_document` check during the common document-loading phase【ev-b56db6f459d806989798†L1851-L1862】.\n\nIt then performs an owner-aware `change_document` check:\n\n```python\nif currentUser is not None and not has_perms_owner_aware(\n    currentUser,\n    \"change_document\",\n    doc,\n):\n    return HttpResponseForbidden(...)\n```\n\n【ev-b56db6f459d806989798†L1877-L1886】\n\nOn success, it creates a `Note` attached to the addressed document, using the submitted `note` value and the current user【ev-b56db6f459d806989798†L1888-L1892】. It may write an audit entry, updates the document's modified timestamp, updates the search backend, and returns the document's notes【ev-b56db6f459d806989798†L1893-L1913】. The protected effect is creation of persistent content on the addressed document, followed by disclosure of the resulting note list.\n\n### Owner/grant branches\n\nFor POST, both object checks matter:\n\n- the common check requires object-aware `view_document`;\n- the POST-specific check requires object-aware `change_document`.\n\nUnder the helper implementation, either check succeeds for an unowned document or when the current user is the owner, without consulting the object grant checker【ev-190e8df9a1f470ae174d†L624-L635】.\n\n| Addressed document state | `view_document` grant | `change_document` grant | Result under source behavior | Supplied-policy result |\n|---|---:|---:|---|---|\n| Owner unspecified | Unspecified | Unspecified | Conditional. If owner is `None`, both owner-aware checks pass without grants; otherwise the result depends on the actual owner and grants. | Must require `change_document`; no ownership/unowned exception is permitted. |\n| Owned by current user | Absent | Absent | The object checks pass because the user is the owner, subject still to the endpoint's model-level permissions. Note creation proceeds. | **Should be denied** absent `change_document`. |\n| Owned by another user | Present | Present | Allowed, subject to endpoint-level model permissions. | Allowed. |\n| Owned by another user | Present | Absent | Denied by the `change_document` object check. | Denied. |\n| Owned by another user | Absent | Present | Denied by the preceding `view_document` object check. | The supplied creation rule expressly requires `change_document`; the source additionally requires `view_document`. Whether that extra prerequisite is intended is not specified by the policy. |\n| Owned by another user | Absent | Absent | Denied by the `view_document` check. | Denied because `change_document` is absent. |\n\n### POST conformance\n\n**Noncompliant for the required creation control.** A current owner can create a note without a `change_document` object grant because ownership satisfies `has_perms_owner_aware`. An unowned document may likewise pass both checks without object grants if `owner is None`.\n\nThe implementation also requires `view_document` for POST, both at the action-level model-permission gate and in the method-level object check【ev-190e8df9a1f470ae174d†L678-L685】【ev-b56db6f459d806989798†L1857-L1862】. The independent policy specifies `change_document` for creation but does not state whether `view_document` is an additional prerequisite. That additional restriction is therefore a **policy gap**, not treated as either compliant or noncompliant with the stated creation requirement.\n\n## Exact gaps and limits\n\n1. **Ownership substitution:** `has_perms_owner_aware` explicitly authorizes the owner without an object grant【ev-190e8df9a1f470ae174d†L624-L635】. This conflicts with the policy for both GET and POST.\n2. **Unowned-document substitution:** The same helper authorizes access when `obj.owner is None`, also without an object grant. The supplied policy does not provide an unowned-document exception.\n3. **GET control mismatch:** GET's relevant object check is `view_document`, which is the correct grant type in name, but it is not mandatory because of the owner/unowned branches.\n4. **POST control mismatch:** POST's relevant mutation check is `change_document`, which is the correct grant type in name, but it is not mandatory because of the owner/unowned branches.\n5. **Additional POST prerequisite:** POST also requires `view_document`. The supplied policy does not say whether creating a note must additionally require viewing permission; source-visible conformance to that extra condition cannot be determined from the supplied policy.\n6. **Unspecified facts:** The document owner and object grants were not supplied. No definitive allow/deny outcome is asserted for those unknown cases beyond the explicit source branches above.\n7. **Scope limit:** This assessment covers only the source-visible GET and POST notes action and its referenced permission helper. It does not infer deployment, router registration details not shown in the evidence, provider behavior, or any permissions outside the supplied policy.\n\n## Smallest effective source correction\n\nAt the last trusted object-authorization decision point, the notes action should use a check whose result is based on the required object grant rather than `owner is None` or `obj.owner == user` shortcuts:\n\n- GET: require object-level `view_document`.\n- POST: require object-level `change_document`.\n\nThe existing endpoint-level model permissions may remain as additional gates, but they must not replace the required addressed-document grant. A regression matrix should cover:\n\n- owner with no grant;\n- non-owner with the required grant;\n- non-owner without the required grant;\n- unowned document with no grant; and\n- POST with `change_document` but without `view_document`, whose expected result requires a policy decision because the supplied policy does not specify that additional prerequisite.","toolCalls":[],"tokens":{"input":6105,"output":2607,"cacheRead":17920,"cacheWrite":0},"costUsd":null,"durationMs":63381.5136,"stopReason":"end_turn"},"endedAt":"2026-09-30T21:15:19.562Z"}}
